AB  - A preregistered chess-training experiment compares automatic AI tips with the same tips plus optional answer-revealing help. Among 216 completers from 306 recruits, the optional-help group had smaller unaided test-score gains after 12 weeks of training. Both randomized groups received AI; the comparison isolates assistance design, not AI versus no AI.
N1  - Stockfish-based chess assistance, not a general-purpose LLM or programming intervention. Main analysis is of completers, with approximately 29% attrition; reported absence of differential attrition does not remove every selection concern. The 30% versus 64% figures are relative changes in bounded test-game scores, not percentages of underlying skill. Causal mediation needs additional assumptions; the nonparticipant comparison is observational.
